From: Codex build workaround <noreply@openai.com>
Subject: [PATCH] libbb: cancel gzip feeder before joining it

When extracting nested ipk archives, the feeder thread may remain blocked in
pipe I/O after the decompressor has been killed.  Joining such a thread can
deadlock the host opkg used by package/install.  Cancellation is safe here:
gzip_close() has already closed the stream and terminated the child process,
and the feeder routine only performs cancellation-point read/write calls.

--- a/libbb/gzip.c
+++ b/libbb/gzip.c
@@ -194,8 +194,10 @@ int gzip_close(struct gzip_handle *zh)
 	if (zh->file)
 		fclose(zh->file);
 
-	if (zh->thread)
+	if (zh->thread) {
+		pthread_cancel(zh->thread);
 		pthread_join(zh->thread, NULL);
+	}
 
 	sigaction(SIGPIPE, &zh->pipe_sa, NULL);
 
